env
# Local env files must never reach the build context. Next.js inlines NEXT_PUBLIC_*
# at build time, so a local .env.local containing NEXT_PUBLIC_SERVER_URL=http://localhost:3000
# bakes localhost into robots.txt, sitemap.xml and metadataBase — verified in a local
# production build. The deploy pipeline supplies real values as build args instead.
#
# The `**/` prefix is load-bearing: a bare `.env.*` matches only a root-level file,
# and the real one lives at apps/web/.env.local. Left unanchored it was still being
# copied in — carrying PAYLOAD_SECRET, SHOPPAGE_AUTH_SECRET, the platform admin
# password and every SHOPPAGE_MERCHANT_SECRET_*. The deploy pipeline supplies real
# values as build args instead.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
